{"source":"github","project_id":"go-snyk-dependency-recursion-issue","target":"rstudio/go-snyk-dependency-recursion-issue","id":"pr/1","ref":1,"title":"add prometheus client_golang to show snyk issue","description":"This commit shows a Snyk issue that reflects the following github issues:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/prometheus/common/issues/223\r\nhttps://github.com/prometheus/client_golang/issues/701\r\n\r\nWe believe that this is a false positive, based on https://github.com/prometheus/common/issues/314#issuecomment-880100105, which states\r\n\r\n\u003e The dependency resolver just finds the most recent of the required versions and uses it.\r\n\r\n(noting of course that this is true within a particular API version scheme, which holds here).","published_at":"2023-02-10T15:24:15Z","updated_at":"2023-03-13T19:41:55Z","url":"https://github.com/rstudio/go-snyk-dependency-recursion-issue/pull/1","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"msarahan","state":"CLOSED"}}
